DEVELOPMENT ONLY -- never applied by the Dockerfiles.

Applies on top of icu/uresdata-frontcode.patch and instruments the two pool
string readers so icu/pin-strings-<icu major>.txt can be regenerated:

  BUN_ICU_TRACE_POOL=<file>  append "<poolPtr>\t<offset>\t<utf8 text>" for
                             every pool string read through the verbatim
                             (non-front-coded) path
  BUN_ICU_TRACE_FC=<file>    append a line per materialized block

Recipe (see also the header of icu/pin-strings-<icu major>.txt): build ICU with the
three icu/*.patch files plus this one; link Bun against that libicuuc and a
package whose pools are NOT front-coded (--pins none produces one); run
  BUN_ICU_TRACE_POOL=/tmp/t.startup  bun -e ''
  BUN_ICU_TRACE_POOL=/tmp/t.firstuse bun <first use of every common Intl API>
and turn the union of the traces into pin lines (tree \t JSON(text)).
For an ICU major Bun does not link (Dockerfile.windows's ICU 73), trace
icu/test-package.cpp's startup phase instead:
  BUN_ICU_TEST_STARTUP_ONLY=1 BUN_ICU_TRACE_POOL=<file> test-package <dat>
Do not feed the wide sweep into the pins: test-package separately asserts
that the front-coded path IS exercised after the startup phase.
